From 466e25e50e9c312b860d785d00336b5a8433fc63 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 16:47:45 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 19/19] Commit Focused Candidate Before Typing

During ordinary conversion, printable continuation input was routed through incremental refinement, so the candidate focused in the window could be lost. Commit that candidate first and feed the same key into a new composition.

Keep source-filtered views incremental because their narrowing workflow depends on retaining the active filter.

Upstream-Commit: 8d132a978c9e9b32daaf556a559bf46da5ed36ec
Downstream-Reason: Restore focused-candidate commit behavior for ordinary candidate continuation while preserving source-filtered narrowing.
Tested-On: macOS arm64; cargo test -p karukan-im

